{
  "id": "page-on-shir-outage",
  "version": "1",
  "lab": "infra",
  "title": "Page the on-call when the self-hosted integration runtime goes down",
  "level": "intermediate",
  "estimate": "30-45 min",
  "skills": [
    "az monitor metrics",
    "metric alert rules",
    "aggregation, window and frequency",
    "action groups",
    "ADF self-hosted IR metrics"
  ],
  "ticket": {
    "from": "Amara Okafor, data platform on-call lead",
    "subject": "Nobody was paged last night",
    "body": [
      "Last night the self-hosted integration runtime on `vm-shir-01` stopped around 02:10 UTC, the orders pipeline",
      "waited in its queue until morning, and we learned it from the sales team at 07:30. `INCIDENT.md` has the",
      "timeline. I want two metric alerts in `rg-integration-prod`, both paging `ag-data-oncall`:",
      "",
      "- **The IR has no available node** (a metric of the data factory `adf-sales-prod`): page within ten minutes",
      "  of the node dropping, severity 1 or more urgent. It must stay silent while the node is up.",
      "- **vm-shir-01 is saturated**: CPU above 90% *sustained*, severity 2 or more urgent. Last night it must have",
      "  fired by 02:30. It must not page for the nightly backup at 01:00, which pegs the CPU for about six minutes.",
      "",
      "Before you tell me it's done, replay last night against your rules (`lab alerts replay`) and read what would",
      "have paged. This is the lab's simulated subscription: the metrics are a recorded scenario, and nothing is",
      "sent to Azure."
    ]
  },
  "acceptance": [
    {
      "id": "node-down",
      "text": "An alert on IntegrationRuntimeAvailableNodeNumber pages ag-data-oncall (sev 0-1) within ten minutes of the outage, and never before.",
      "checks": [
        {
          "kind": "azure_alert",
          "scope": "adf-sales-prod",
          "metric": "IntegrationRuntimeAvailableNodeNumber",
          "max_severity": 1,
          "action_group": "ag-data-oncall",
          "fires": [
            [
              "2026-10-05T02:12:00Z",
              "2026-10-05T02:22:00Z"
            ]
          ],
          "quiet": [
            [
              "2026-10-04T09:00:00Z",
              "2026-10-05T02:11:59Z"
            ]
          ],
          "fail": "The node alert would not have paged as the ticket asks:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cpu-sustained",
      "text": "A sustained-CPU alert on vm-shir-01 pages ag-data-oncall (sev 0-2) by 02:30, and stays silent for the 01:00 backup.",
      "checks": [
        {
          "kind": "azure_alert",
          "scope": "vm-shir-01",
          "metric": "Percentage CPU",
          "max_severity": 2,
          "action_group": "ag-data-oncall",
          "fires": [
            [
              "2026-10-05T02:05:00Z",
              "2026-10-05T02:30:00Z"
            ]
          ],
          "quiet": [
            [
              "2026-10-05T00:45:00Z",
              "2026-10-05T01:45:00Z"
            ]
          ],
          "fail": "The CPU alert would not have paged as the ticket asks:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "replayed",
      "text": "You replayed last night against your rules after their last change.",
      "checks": [
        {
          "kind": "journal",
          "includes": [
            "^lab alerts replay"
          ],
          "before": [
            [
              "^az monitor metrics alert (create|update)",
              "^lab alerts replay"
            ]
          ],
          "fail": "The rules were not replayed after their last change."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "`az monitor metrics list-definitions --resource adf-sales-prod` lists the metrics of the data factory; the IR ones start with IntegrationRuntime.",
    "Look at last night first: `az monitor metrics list --resource vm-shir-01 --metric \"Percentage CPU\" --interval 5m --start-time 2026-10-05T00:30:00Z --end-time 2026-10-05T03:30:00Z`.",
    "A metric alert aggregates the metric over the window (`--window-size`) every `--evaluation-frequency`: `avg` over 15 minutes ignores a six-minute spike; `max` over any window does not.",
    "The condition is one string: `--condition \"avg Percentage CPU > 90\"`. `--action ag-data-oncall` routes it; `--severity 0` is the most urgent.",
    "Changed your mind? `az monitor metrics alert update -n NAME -g rg-integration-prod --window-size 15m`, or delete it and create it again. Then `lab alerts replay`."
  ],
